  "functions": [
    "FUNC.INTERCEPT"
  ],
  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "INTERCEPT evaluates mean_y - slope * mean_x in plain binary64 using two-pass means and SLOPE's centered quotient",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20131 and 20527, INTERCEPT(known_y's, known_x's) validates singleton blank/error arguments in formula order (#VALUE! on a blank singleton before inspecting known_x's), returns #N/A on shape mismatch, skips positions where either argument holds text, logical, or blank, and computes mean_y - slope * mean_x in plain binary64 arithmetic where slope is sum((x - mean_x)*(y - mean_y)) / sum((x - mean_x)^2) from two-pass sample means, returning #DIV/0! when fewer than 2 numeric pairs exist or sum((x - mean_x)^2) == 0. Matches 2,856/2,856 full-bank and 4/4 pinned INTERCEPT rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20131 (4/4 pinned rows in witnesses/INTERCEPT.json) and Excel 16.0.20527 (2,856/2,856 full-bank INTERCEPT rows and prefix_metadata row 136).",
